---
title: "Print and archive tags or documents"
sidebar:
  order: 8
---

Produce physical outputs while retaining a reproducible digital copy.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Preview the PDF against representative records and the intended paper or tag stock.
2. Save the final PDF with the project name, output type, and date.
3. Print a small test and check dimensions, margins, legibility, identifiers, and duplex orientation.
4. Print the production set and compare a sample with the source records.
5. Archive the PDF, matching template, print layout, and relevant user configuration with the project backup.
{% /steps %}

Print at actual size when label dimensions must match the layout, and verify one sheet before printing the full set.

